# `__GAME_ID__` (solo score chase) — build checklist

Stamped by `pnpm new-game __GAME_ID__ --solo chase`. Work through this in order — it doubles
as the CLAUDE.md §2 loop's stage-2 (Develop) TDD anchor list for this game.

## Traps every new engine hits (read before you touch `engine.ts`)

1. **`Move` needs an explicit index signature.** A `Move` type used as the engine's `M`
   generic must satisfy `Json`, and TypeScript will **not** synthesize a `[key: string]: Json`
   index signature for a plain `interface`/type-literal — you must write it yourself (see
   `__PASCAL_ID__Move` in `engine.ts`).
2. **`encode` must exclude `lastEffects`.** Two states identical except for effects must hash
   identically. If effects ever leak into the canonical encoding, positions that are the same
   in every way the rules care about will hash differently — silently, with no failing test.
3. **If legality depends on the PATH taken, not the position reached, `encode` is NOT a valid
   position key** (platform-corrections.md C3). This template's placeholder is path-independent
   (`encode` = `{score, moves}` is a sound key), but check this against your REAL mechanic —
   it changes which solver-building-blocks are safe to compose.
4. **`decode` must throw on malformed input, never return a partial state**
   (platform-corrections.md C4). `decode` feeds `replay()` and `verifyCertificate` — the
   platform's trust boundary for a submitted move log or a shipped daily. Keep this property
   no matter how much richer your real state gets.

## Score-chase-specific

- **`probes.ts`'s `safeMove` is MANDATORY, not optional.** `runAlwaysSafeProbe` hard-errors
  (`MissingSafeMoveError`) without one — the Always-Safe gate ("is the risk in
  press-your-luck real?") cannot run without it, and a chase manifest without it cannot pass
  CI, by design. Do not delete `probes.ts`.
- **Structural termination is mandatory.** `manifest.solo.moveCap` (default 2000) is a
  tripwire, not your ending — your `status()` must have a real terminal condition
  independent of it.
- **`score()` must equal `status().scores[0]` at the scored terminal**, and if you set
  `solo.scoreMonotone: true` in `manifest.ts`, it must never decrease (testkit-asserted once
  your terminal is real).

## Build order

- [ ] `engine.ts` — replace `computeStatus`'s TODO with your real terminal condition.
      `pnpm --filter @twist-arcade/__GAME_ID__ test` should turn the "termination" failure
      green.
- [ ] `engineContract` green — the solo branch (score-chase terminals only: `scored` — never
      `won`/`lost`/`draw`) is auto-checked because `maxPlayers === 1`.
- [ ] `probes.ts` — a REAL `safeMove` (the minimum-variance option for your mechanic).
- [ ] `manifest.ts` — fill in `title`, `classic`, `ruleSentence` (<=90 chars — asserted for
      real in `manifest.test.ts`), `tags`, `estMinutes`; tune `solo.moveCap` and confirm
      `scoreMonotone`.
- [ ] `pnpm harness suite __GAME_ID__ --suite solo-ci` green (Strong/Random ratio,
      distribution overlap, Greedy/Random, Strong/Greedy, Strong CV, Always-Safe-vs-Strong,
      Grind probe, run-length band, cap-hit rate, ceiling pile-up).
- [ ] `pnpm harness suite __GAME_ID__ --suite solo-design` reviewed (tighter bands, Fable
      stage-3/6 — CI proves not-broken, design decides good).
- [ ] `ui/Board.tsx` + the grayscale-screenshot test (every state change must read from a
      static, colorless render — motion may only restate it, per C5).
- [ ] `index.ts`'s `announce()` strings — real per-event sentence fragments (ux-lens §9).
- [ ] `shareArtifact()` — <=7 lines, emoji move-timeline body only.
- [ ] `howSheetFrames` — three real frames.
- [ ] Register in `games/registry.ts` (the scaffold already inserted your entry at the
      `<new-game:insert>` marker — confirm it and delete this line once you have).
- [ ] Open the PR — CLAUDE.md §2's loop (stage 3 onward) takes it from here.
